> Original1009 witness and1001 composite control

Retain n=1009, whose predecessor factors as1008=2^4*3^2*7. The actual least
accepted witness is11. Its full-exponent residue is1, and the proper-order
residues for q=2,3,7 are1008,374,935. The complete factorization and all actual
base outcomes are native results. A separate1001=7*11*13 control produces a
genuine Fermat failure and can stop immediately; continuing to try every
remaining base would add work without changing its conclusive composite result.

All modular-power calls use the canonical full-width unsigned implementation
with128-bit products. Trial division tests d<=remaining/d instead of forming a
potentially overflowing d*d. Factoring n−1 is part of the algorithm’s actual
cost and must finish before a Lucas prime certificate is possible.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lucas_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lucas_primality_trace(1009);
    std::print("| actual prime factor | actual extracted multiplicity |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &f : t.analysis.factors)
        std::print("| {} | {} |\n", f.prime, f.exponent);
    std::print("\n| actual base | Fermat passed | actual first rejected factor0 means none | actual " "accepted |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | --- |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (auto &a : t.bases) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", a.base, a.fermat_passed,
                   a.rejected_factor, a.accepted);
        x.push_back(a.base);
        y.push_back(a.accepted);
    }
    auto c = dm::algorithms::lucas_primality_analyze(1001);
    std::print("\nActual1009 witness {}; actual powers {}; actual trial-divisor tests {};1001 conclusive " "{}; prime {}; Fermat-failing base {}.\n",
               t.analysis.witness, t.analysis.work.powers,
               t.analysis.work.trial_divisors, c.conclusive, c.prime,
               c.composite_base);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual acceptance", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(-.1, 1.5).title("Original1009: actual increasing base outcomes").x_label("actual examined base").y_label("full-order witness accepted: one=yes").save_svg("build/lucas_original.svg");
}
```
