> Least accepted witnesses through three hundred

The original figure plotted the least primitive-root witness for each prime
from3 through300. The native census now runs the actual bounded producer for
every prescribed integer, then the report selects its conclusive prime results
for presentation. No report-local primality sieve, trial factorization, modular
exponentiation or duplicate smallest-witness search is used. The plotted witness
is the actual first accepted base in increasing order, not an arbitrary
successful base.

These observed small witnesses are a feature of this bounded interval, not a
general small-witness guarantee. The special prime2 has witness sentinel1 and
needs no factorization/search; it is explicitly excluded from the original3..300
plot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lucas_census.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto census = dm::algorithms::lucas_primality_census(3, 300);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual conclusive prime | actual least accepted witness | actual examined bases | actual " "power calls |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &a : census)
        if (a.conclusive && a.prime) {
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", a.n, a.witness, a.work.bases,
                       a.work.powers);
    x.push_back(a.n);
    y.push_back(a.witness);
        }
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.points(x, y, "actual least witness", {37, 99, 235}, 5).title(
            "Original interval: actual least Lucas witnesses").x_label(
            "conclusive prime candidate").y_label("actual first accepted base").save_svg("build/lucas_census.svg");
}
```
